@echo off
rem STARTUP.CMD lines for the QCA6174 / QCA9377 driver.
rem The driver cannot read files during boot, so the two ath10k firmware files (linux-firmware) are copied into it
rem once per boot: QCA6174 from ath10k/QCA6174/hw3.0/, QCA9377 from ath10k/QCA9377/hw1.0/ (see bin\firmware\).
rem Board file first or firmware first: either order. Use the folder of YOUR card.
copy /b C:\IBMCOM\MACS\QCA6174\firmware-6.bin \DEV\WRND32$ > nul
copy /b C:\IBMCOM\MACS\QCA6174\board-2.bin \DEV\WRND32$ > nul
rem ORDER MATTERS: these two lines must run BEFORE the supplicant / Wireless LAN Monitor starts. If the firmware is
rem copied after that, the adapter has no MAC address yet (00:00:00:00:00:00) and the 4-way handshake fails.
rem The MAC address is only known after the firmware runs, which is after the protocol stack has bound, so set
rem NETADDRESS = "xxxxxxxxxxxx" under [QCA6174_NIF] in PROTOCOL.INI (install\QCMAC.CMD does it once) and reboot.
rem The adapter starts as soon as both files are copied. The state can be read at any time:  copy \DEV\WRND32$ con
